t so i actually did  like the bags obviously his standup is  not quite as popular as his podcast but  saying that joe rogan is just a  podcaster not a good comedian makes no  sense to me still in that small  percentage of people that can sell out  arenas all across the country i was  laughing the whole show every joke hit  it was a great show granted i was super  drunk so that might have had something  to do with it but i thought it was  hilarious the show was supposed to start  at eight we got to the arena around 7  50. the lines were out the door  obviously but it didn't take that long  to get in they put your phone in the  magnetic bags and then we went to our  seats probably sat down around 8 15. the  first comic didn't come out till about  nine so there was an hour there where we  had nothing to do our phones were locked  up so all we could do was keep drinking  so we were pounding beers during that by  the time the show started everyone is  just trash in the whole arena twenty  thousand people ready to see joe rogan  pack crowd no masks it was great it was  so dope laura beets was the first opener  she did great she killed it i had to pee  during her whole set i had been drinking  all day i already broke the seal but  then she brought tony hinchcliffe and  the place went nuts i had no idea tony  was going to be there so that was a  treat he was dressed like a cowboy came  out he murdered he talked about getting  canceled talked about moving to texas  he was completely unfiltered with the  phones in the bags he was amazing and i  still depe during that whole set but  then he immediately brought out joe  rogan so there was no break and i didn't  want to miss a second of that so i had  to sit there for rogan's whole hour set  having to piss my pants but also  laughing really hard at the jokes there  was a good 20 minutes where i was  considering peeing in one of my beer  cans but i you know there were too many  people right next to me i didn't want  this the spra